WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.800
Whether you're a longtime fan of Kate Kane
or relatively new to the character, you've

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.100
come to the right place.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.080
Here's what we know about The CW's upcoming
Arrowverse superhero show Batwoman : who's

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.520
in it, what it's about, and why you should
start getting excited.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.440
“I’m going to Gotham City.”

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.680
Batwoman is set to premiere on October 6th,
2019, followed by the fifth season premiere

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.700
of Supergirl, serving up a double dose of
DC's most badass women.

00:00:26.929 --> 00:00:31.040
If you're looking to catch up before she sets
off on her own adventures, Batwoman has already

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.920
appeared on a few of the CW's other superhero
shows.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.420
She appeared in the Elseworlds crossover event,
which played out across episodes of Arrow,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.769
The Flash, and Supergirl in December of 2018,
and served to introduce Ruby Rose's take on

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:45.260
the character to the TV audience.

00:00:45.949 --> 00:00:50.300
We aren't sure how tied into these shows Batwoman
will be since that crossover involved dipping

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:55.250
into alternate universes, but being set on
parallel worlds hasn't stopped the Flash and

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.000
Supergirl from hanging out, so it might be
worth checking in.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:02.480
One of the big reveals there was that while
Batman does exist in the version of Gotham

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.870
City that we're seeing in Batwoman, the Dark
Knight has been mysteriously absent for quite

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.980
some time, leaving a vigilante void and a
city full of super-criminals.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.280
Right from the start, the odds are stacked
against Batwoman, but clearly, she's up for

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:15.780
the task.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:21.940
The CW has released a ton of footage for Batwoman
online, but in May, we got a "First Look"

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:25.020
trailer that might just give us the best idea
of what we can expect.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.000
Right away, we're introduced to "The Crows,"
Gotham City's private mercenary police force,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.300
established in the wake of Batman's departure.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.960
It appears they aren't quite as effective
as the Batman, however, as they are quickly

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.480
picked off by Batwoman's central antagonist:
Alice, a ruthless criminal and Lewis Carroll

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:41.980
fan.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.940
Rachel Skarsten looks like she's really enjoying
the role of the unhinged Alice, which should

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.400
make her a fun villain to watch.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.640
There's a long history of DC characters who
have gone by the name "Batwoman," but the

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.220
one we know today, Kate Kane, has only existed
for a little over a decade, having first appeared

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.500
in 2006.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:04.040
In the comics, Kate Kane is Bruce Wayne's
cousin, but her childhood was arguably even

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.120
worse than his.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:10.320
At the age of 12, she was kidnapped by a cult
alongside her mother, Gabrielle, and twin

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:10.900
sister, Beth.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.580
The cult murdered Gabrielle and seemingly
Beth as well, with Kate as a witness to the

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.140
tragedy, giving her a similar trauma to her
famous bat-relative.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.200
As an adult, Kate went through West Point,
hoping to join the Army, but was kicked out

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.620
under "Don't Ask Don't Tell" as a lesbian.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:30.920
She was inspired to continue to fight for
justice by Batman himself, using fear to intimidate

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.680
criminals, but operating mostly on her own
using her military training and technology.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.540
It could be easy to dismiss Alice as "Batwoman's
Joker," because… well, that's basically

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.440
what she is.

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:47.700
She is a Gotham crime boss commanding a massive
web of criminals, and she's more than a bit

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.380
unhinged.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.100
She's also a skilled fighter.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.740
"Welcome back to Gotham Kate.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:56.040
We’re all mad here."

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.310
She's obsessed with Alice in Wonderland, though
her comics iteration is not tied to the Mad

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.600
Hatter or his gang.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.150
The comics have a few interesting twists about
the connection between Alice and Batwoman

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.900
no spoilers for the uninitiated, but we'll
see if the show picks those up.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.940
While we know a few of the characters we can
expect to see, the CW is keeping a pretty

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.400
tight lid on the plot of Batwoman's first
season.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:22.880
Obviously, we're going to see Kate Kane's
transformation into Gotham's protector, and

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:26.680
judging from the trailer, it seems like Alice
is going to be the villain who forces her

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.560
into becoming Gotham City's new bat-themed
hero.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:34.160
Along with Alice, the CW has confirmed that
two other comic villains are coming to the

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.640
first season of Batwoman, but we don't know
how big a role they'll play.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:42.660
Magpie, who was also used as a minor villain
in the final season of Gotham, will be showing

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.240
up in at least one episode.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.260
Season one will also introduce Tommy Elliot,
who later becomes Hush.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.780
We can also expect a few ties between Batwoman
and the larger Batman universe.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.240
For example, Kate Kane's tech guru is the
son of Lucius Fox.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:04:00.820
That said, it seems unlikely that the Dark
Knight will ever appear in Batwoman… at

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.460
least for a while.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.220
Ruby Rose has played plenty of badass characters
before stepping into the role of Batwoman.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.880
The Australian actress is probably best known
for Orange is the New Black, but she's also

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:17.420
shown up in plenty of other big time action
franchises like xXx and John Wick.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:22.820
Rose is interesting casting in a lot of ways,
but one particularly noteworthy piece is that

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.699
Rose, who identifies as genderfluid and a
lesbian, is playing the first openly gay superhero

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.780
lead to come to film or television.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.530
A huge part of Batwoman's origin story is
her dismissal from West Point after being

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.020
outed.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:40.240
Rather than avoid this aspect of the character,
The CW is fully embracing it, putting Kate

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.840
Kane's sexuality front and center.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.749
Ruby Rose has spoken extensively about her
struggles with identity growing up, and how

00:04:46.749 --> 00:04:49.900
she hopes she can be a positive influence
through her success.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:53.940
She's said in interviews that she wants Batwoman
to be the kind of show that would've made

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.210
her life better if she'd had it when she was
a teenager, showing a hero who can make some

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:00.320
changes in the real world, too.

